 the evidence underscores the complexity of polypharmacy in psychiatric care.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Other drug classes relevant to psychiatric care show distinct risk profiles\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Drug classes such as Class III antiarrhythmics and antiparkinsonian agents appear in the network due to their interactions or adverse effects relevant to psychiatric patients. Class III antiarrhythmics interact with quinolone antibiotics to increase QT prolongation risk [Data: Relationships (33337)], while antiparkinsonian drugs can cause hyperthermia when combined with phenothiazines [Data: Relationships (11951)]. These findings illustrate how non-psychiatric medications commonly used in comorbid conditions can significantly impact the safety of psychiatric treatment regimens.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community presents a moderate-to-high impact severity due to the presence of multiple high-risk drug interactions, contraindications in vulnerable populations, and associations with serious adverse reactions like QT prolongation.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126700, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1416, "prompt_tokens": 6318, "total_tokens": 7734, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Amisulpride and Related Psychiatric Medication Network\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on the antipsychotic drug amisulpride (氨磺必利) and its relationships with psychiatric conditions, drug classes, and potential drug interactions. Amisulpride is indicated